{"author":{"id":"8d7a7fea5b07a0d5d081edd516d55afeb51ce9c18b2b2be6ceb30eb17cd9b547"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794289236,"nonce":"nBYjcsVNZqRuXf/M14GK7dz1X7U=","title":"cn::input cannot take a height: InputSize fixes it at 32, 40 or 48 px","message":"`blinc_cn::components::input` sets `.h(config.size.height(theme))` from `InputSize` (Small 32, Medium 40, Large 48, from spacing tokens) and has no `height()` on `InputBuilder`. A style with its own control height (macOS regular 22 px, Windows 32 px, large touch style 56 px) cannot use it.\n\n`blinc_layout::widgets::text_input::text_input` takes any height (`.h()`), text size, radius, border and colours, so we build on that and lose the cn label/description/error wrapper. Measured: controls of 22, 32, 44 and 56 px come out at exactly those heights.\n\nWanted: `InputBuilder::height(f32)` (and text size) that overrides the size's value.","files":null}]}